WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:19.527
When I came down to breakfast, Uncle Silas and Aunt Sally were sitting at the table, looking sad.

2
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.148
Then, we all heard noises in the yard and ran outside.

3
00:00:24.128 --> 00:00:24.749
It was Tom!

4
00:00:25.229 --> 00:00:28.090
The doctor and some other men were carrying him on a mattress.

5
00:00:29.091 --> 00:00:32.252
Jim was there, too, with his hands tied behind his back.

6
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:35.985
He was surrounded by the men who had chased us two nights ago.

7
00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:42.767
Aunt Sally became very busy, giving orders to servants and getting a bed ready for Tom.

8
00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:46.668
Meanwhile, the men were treating Jim roughly.

9
00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:51.269
One of them even said he should be hanged because of the trouble he had caused.

10
00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:57.691
But another man said, no, the slave didn't belong to them, and his owner would be very angry

11
00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.351
if he didn't get his property back.

12
00:01:00.811 --> 00:01:02.512
Jim pretended that he didn't know me.

13
00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:05.589
I felt terribly sad that I couldn't help him.

14
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.852
I was very relieved when the doctor told the men to treat him kindly.

15
00:01:09.872 --> 00:01:12.793
"He's a good man," the doctor said.

16
00:01:12.813 --> 00:01:16.516
"He could have run away, but he stayed with me the whole time.

17
00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:20.298
He was a good nurse to that boy and helped me save his life."

18
00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:27.542
After that the men were kinder to Jim, but they still put chains on him and locked him

19
00:01:27.582 --> 00:01:28.262
in the shed again.

20
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:31.344
The doctor told me that Tom was going to be fine.

21
00:01:32.428 --> 00:01:34.669
But I knew I still had a lot to worry about.

22
00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:39.330
How would I explain why I didn't tell the Phelpses that Sid was shot?

23
00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.611
How could I help to free Jim?

24
00:01:44.652 --> 00:01:48.533
The next day, Tom was so much better that I was allowed to go see him in his

25
00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:53.314
room. He was sitting up in bed, and he began to talk to me and Aunt Sally.

26
00:01:54.255 --> 00:01:57.996
He was not very alert after his gunshot wound and his fever.

27
00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:02.825
I quickly realized he had forgotten that we were keeping many things secret.

28
00:02:02.845 --> 00:02:05.046
"How's Jim?"

29
00:02:05.686 --> 00:02:06.266
he said to me.

30
00:02:06.286 --> 00:02:11.667
"He's fine," I said quietly, frowning at him to show that he should be quiet.

31
00:02:12.388 --> 00:02:13.428
But he kept on talking.

32
00:02:13.448 --> 00:02:16.769
"Have you told Aunt Sally how we did everything?"

33
00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.129
continued Tom.

34
00:02:18.149 --> 00:02:20.090
"Did what?"

35
00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.850
asked Aunt Sally, looking suspicious.

36
00:02:24.131 --> 00:02:30.113
Then, Tom told the whole story: the escape plan, the things we borrowed, the tunnel we had dug.

37
00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:32.835
Aunt Sally was astonished.

38
00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:38.158
When she realized how much trouble we had caused, she started to look angry.

39
00:02:39.039 --> 00:02:40.200
But Tom kept smiling.

40
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.923
and so we helped the runaway slave get away," he finished.

41
00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:49.586
"But he didn't get away," said Aunt Sally.

42
00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:52.188
"He's locked in the shed right now."

43
00:02:53.088 --> 00:02:54.569
Tom's face grew red.

44
00:02:54.589 --> 00:02:56.631
"No, that's not right!

45
00:02:57.031 --> 00:02:58.032
You have to let him go.

46
00:02:59.128 --> 00:02:59.688
Old Mrs.

47
00:02:59.789 --> 00:03:04.191
Watson died two months ago, and in her will, she set Jim free.

48
00:03:05.371 --> 00:03:08.133
He's a free man, as free as you and me!"

49
00:03:10.094 --> 00:03:14.396
Aunt Sally opened her mouth to speak, when someone else hurried into the room.

50
00:03:14.416 --> 00:03:16.818
"Why, sister!"

51
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:18.138
she exclaimed.

52
00:03:18.839 --> 00:03:21.640
I turned to look, and there was Tom's Aunt Polly!

53
00:03:22.721 --> 00:03:26.002
While the two sisters were hugging, I hid under the bed.

54
00:03:26.022 --> 00:03:28.724
"Come out from there, Huck Finn!"

55
00:03:29.428 --> 00:03:30.569
commanded Aunt Polly.

56
00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:34.770
"What mischief have you and Tom been making now?"

57
00:03:35.731 --> 00:03:37.451
Aunt Sally was very confused.

58
00:03:37.471 --> 00:03:41.933
"But that's Tom under the bed, and Sid in the bed!"

59
00:03:41.953 --> 00:03:49.076
"I certainly know my own nephew Tom—I've looked after him since he was a baby," said Aunt Polly.

60
00:03:49.096 --> 00:03:51.697
"And I know Huckleberry, too!

61
00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:57.260
When I got that letter from you saying Sid was visiting, I had to come and see what

62
00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:57.900
was wrong.

63
00:03:59.068 --> 00:04:01.290
Sid is safe at home, where he should be."

64
00:04:03.912 --> 00:04:08.396
The first chance I got to talk to Tom by himself, I asked him why he never told

65
00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:09.737
us that Jim was a free man.

66
00:04:09.757 --> 00:04:13.561
"I wanted to have adventures," Tom said.

67
00:04:13.581 --> 00:04:15.923
"I wanted to free him from prison.

68
00:04:16.763 --> 00:04:20.567
Then, I wanted to go down the Mississippi on the raft with you and him.

69
00:04:21.548 --> 00:04:25.331
I planned to wait until we got to New Orleans and then tell Jim the truth."

70
00:04:26.876 --> 00:04:31.139
Aunt Sally and Uncle Silas freed Jim from the shed as soon as they heard Tom's story.

71
00:04:32.559 --> 00:04:35.441
They fed him a good meal and gave him some clean clothes.

72
00:04:36.521 --> 00:04:39.363
Then Tom gave Jim forty dollars to start his new life.

73
00:04:39.383 --> 00:04:42.445
"Remember what I told you, Huck?"

74
00:04:43.025 --> 00:04:43.765
Jim said to me.

75
00:04:43.785 --> 00:04:48.808
"If a man has hair on his chest like me, it means he is going to be rich

76
00:04:48.848 --> 00:04:49.288
some day.

77
00:04:49.809 --> 00:04:50.829
And now I am!"

78
00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:55.572
Once Tom was feeling better, he wanted Jim to stay for a few days.

79
00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.262
"We could dress up and pretend to be pirates," Tom suggested.

80
00:05:00.282 --> 00:05:03.264
"I don't have any money for pirate clothes.

81
00:05:04.164 --> 00:05:07.766
I guess by now Pap got all our money from Judge Thatcher," I said.

82
00:05:09.247 --> 00:05:11.308
"No, he hasn't," said Tom.

83
00:05:11.328 --> 00:05:13.830
"We still have our six thousand dollars.

84
00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.032
Pap hasn't come back—at least, he hadn't when I left home."

85
00:05:19.713 --> 00:05:24.356
Then, Jim said in a serious voice, "Your Pap isn't ever coming back, Huck.

86
00:05:24.852 --> 00:05:26.473
You don't have to worry about that."

87
00:05:27.733 --> 00:05:33.174
At first, he didn't want to explain how he knew this, but I wouldn't stop asking questions.

88
00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:39.516
Finally Jim said, "Do you remember that house that we found, floating down the river?"

89
00:05:40.636 --> 00:05:41.057
I nodded.

90
00:05:42.137 --> 00:05:46.058
"Do you remember that there was a body inside, and I told you not to look?

91
00:05:47.278 --> 00:05:50.639
Well, I recognized his face—it was your Pap."

92
00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.201
Well, now I've finished everything I wanted to write.

93
00:05:57.102 --> 00:05:58.142
Tom's leg has healed.

94
00:05:58.622 --> 00:06:00.463
And he kept the bullet for a souvenir.

95
00:06:01.584 --> 00:06:04.425
Aunt Sally wants to adopt me and civilize me.

96
00:06:05.406 --> 00:06:06.386
But I might run away.

97
00:06:07.026 --> 00:06:10.288
I've already been civilized once, and I don't think I like it.
